messages.content:
Retry GO-01 as exactly one inspectable structured change proposal. Do not apply it.

Use the eight existing source question and decision records already supplied in the editable context. Add exactly eight separate unresolved production follow-up questions—one add patch per new question—using only the explicitly authorized collection insertion target in objectPointers.collectionInsertions.questions: operation add, path /questions/-.

For each new question:

- provide a unique, stable, readable question_... ID;
- use only fields allowed by editableContext.supportedSchemas.question;
- set status to open and use the appropriate supported classification;
- state in whyItMatters which existing source question and decision it follows from, since the question schema has no dedicated linkage fields;
- keep the production issue unresolved—do not copy a prototype answer into answer or treat an approved prototype assumption as a production decision;
- do not create a duplicate of any current open question.

Preserve every existing question, decision, requirement, flow, screen, ID, status, acceptance item and discussion record. Preserve the GO-02 and GO-03 corrections. Do not replace the whole questions array. Set proposal impact arrays for requirements, flows and screens to empty because these additions are tracking-only and do not alter design contracts.

Before returning the proposal, verify that its base revision is the supplied current blueprint revision, that it contains exactly eight patches, and that every patch is add /questions/- with one complete valid question object. If any required source object, supported field or authorized insertion target is missing, return proposal: null and identify the exact missing evidence instead of guessing.
